course: dictionary
lesson: 7268
title: One word, many meanings: pillar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word pillar can mean a strong post that holds up a building, or it can mean an important person or idea that supports a group. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «He had messages carved on rocks and tall pillars across India» tells you the pillars are stone posts, because you carve messages into stone.
explain: «There are passages and rooms everywhere, pillars, arches and stone floors.» The words arches and stone floors are clues. They tell you the pillars are part of a building. A pillar of smoke, fire or cloud is a tall column of it, so the word can also describe something tall and thin in the sky.
explain: When a word has several meanings, try each one in the sentence and see which one makes sense. Swap in post or column: «a stone post holds up the roof» works, so the first meaning fits. For the word pillar, the clues always lead you to the right meaning.
fact: A pillar is a tall, strong post of stone, wood or metal.
fact: A pillar of smoke, fire or cloud is a tall column of it.
fact: A pillar of a community is an important person or idea that supports it: a pillar of the church.
fact: «From pillar to post» is a UK phrase meaning from one place to another without rest.
fact: «Ashoka's lion pillar» is today a national emblem of India. The Five Pillars of Islam are five key duties of the religion.
exercise: «He had messages carved on rocks and tall pillars across India.» What is a pillar in this sentence? | *A tall stone post | A puddle of water | A small bird | A type of cake
exercise: «The Five Pillars are: the declaration of faith, prayer five times a day, giving to the poor, fasting in Ramadan and the pilgrimage to Mecca.» How many pillars are there? | Three | *Five | Ten | Seven
exercise: Ella says the head teacher is a pillar of the school. What does this mean? | A person who is always late | A tall stone post in the playground | A type of school bag | *An important person who supports the school
test: «A plant is built like a house with plumbing: the stem is a bundle of pipes and a pillar.» In this sentence, pillar most likely means | *A strong support that holds the plant up | A friend who helps | A sort of fruit | A lamp
test: What does the UK phrase «from pillar to post» mean? | *From one place to another without rest | Standing still on a tall stone post | Very quiet and gentle | Happy and in good spirits all day
exam: «Ashoka's lion pillar» is today what? | Lost in the desert | A famous pizza | *A national emblem of India | A type of boat
